@page "/tw/tree"

<PageTitle>Tree View (Tailwind) · Bheadless</PageTitle>

<div class="bb-intro">
    <h1>Tree View</h1>
    <p class="bb-subtitle">A hierarchical list — file explorers, navigation, nested settings — with expand / collapse, single, multiple and checkbox selection, lazy loading and typeahead.</p>
</div>

<SectionSwitcher Slug="tree" />

<TwDemoBlock Title="File explorer" Code="@_explorerCode">
    <Description>
        The WAI-ARIA Tree View pattern. Click a row to select it (<code>@@bind-SelectedValue</code>) or
        the chevron (<code>BitBhTreeItemToggle</code>) to expand without selecting. Keyboard: Up / Down move,
        Right expands or enters a folder, Left collapses or returns to the parent, Home / End jump,
        <code>*</code> expands every sibling, Enter (or double click) fires <code>OnItemActivate</code>,
        and typing a name jumps to it (typeahead, matched against <code>Label</code>).
        <code>aria-level</code>, <code>aria-setsize</code>, <code>aria-posinset</code> and the roving
        <code>tabindex</code> are computed for you; disabled items are skipped. Each item's
        <code>&lt;li&gt;</code> wraps its children, so state is styled on the item's own row through a child
        combinator — the CSS version with <code>.tree-item[aria-selected="true"] &gt; .tree-row</code>, the
        Tailwind version with <code>[&amp;_[aria-selected=true]&gt;div]:</code> on the tree root — which keeps a
        selected folder from tinting its children.
    </Description>
    <LiveContent>
        <div class="flex w-full flex-col items-start gap-3">
            <BitBhTree TValue="string" aria-label="Project files"
                    @bind-SelectedValue="selectedFile"
                    DefaultExpandedValues="@(new[] { "src/", "src/components/" })"
